-- title:
--   Subgroup ideals of a formal group law are invariantly generated
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B$ in the sense of the project structure `FormalODModule`, that is, a $2$-dimensional commutative formal group law $F$ over $B$ equipped with an action of $\mathrm{Zp2}\,p$ by endomorphisms of the law and a further endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ a = \mathrm{Frob}(a)\circ\varpi$; only the underlying law $F$ enters the statement, through its two power series $F_i \in B[\![x_1,x_2,y_1,y_2]\!]$. Let $I \subseteq B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ be an ideal such that $B[\![x]\!]/I$ is a finite free $B$-module, such that for some $q$ both $x_1^q$ and $x_2^q$ lie in $I$, such that every $f \in I$ has vanishing constant coefficient, and such that $I$ is a subgroup ideal: for every $f \in I$, the series $f(F(x,y))$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by the union of $I(x)$ and $I(y)$, the images of $I$ under the two substitutions $x_i \mapsto x_i$ and $x_i \mapsto y_i$. The conclusion is that $I$ is the ideal generated by the set of its invariant elements, namely those $w \in I$ with $w(F(x,y)) - w(x)$ in the ideal generated by $I(y)$.
--
--   The statement expresses the torsor property of the quotient of a two-dimensional formal group law by a finite free infinitesimal subgroup scheme: the ring of invariant functions $R$ cuts out the subgroup, so that $I = (R \cap I)\,B[\![x]\!]$. It feeds the construction of explicit free generators of such subgroup ideals, being used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_notMem_free_and_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal_of_isMaximal`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_notMem_free_and_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal_of_isMaximal).
